  },
  "construction": {
    "basis": "reconstruction",
    "fidelity": "not-applicable",
    "note": "The finished design was read from Wichmann’s P183 drawing, whose pieces are drawn edge to edge. Each ten-pointed star is two regular pentagons. The stars stand in columns, with regular decagons between the columns. The stars sit at the centre and the corners of a rectangle 2(2 + √5) by 2 tan 54° in units of the star’s radius (drawing within 0.002), the frame of Mirza Akber’s sheet 31, whose opening this shares. Every other line is a parallel to a line of the star through a crossing of earlier lines. The drawing gives no steps; we devised the construction.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. Colours follow his drawing, by shape. No photograph was checked.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-27"
  },
  "credits": [
    {
